  "security_implications": "sp_enc_err_q latches an error condition and is only cleared by reset. Once set, it stays high regardless of sp_enc_err_d deassertion. If this error flag gates encryption operations or influences security-critical controls, a single injected fault could permanently disable the module until a system-wide reset, which may be exploited for a denial-of-service attack or to suppress later error reporting.",
